  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent low-bias: model underestimates the true path during the upswing regime. Apply an upward level shift that grows with horizon (small at days 1–5, larger by days 10–30).",
    "Trend/lag error: forecasts react too slowly to turning points (especially the mid-period rally). Add a momentum term: if the last 5–10 days show positive slope, tilt the whole forecast path upward; if negative slope, tilt downward.",
    "Damped amplitude: model’s peaks/troughs are too muted versus realized moves. Increase volatility scaling (widen forecast swings) rather than pulling strongly back to the recent mean.",
    "Horizon-specific underpricing: the largest errors occur beyond ~day 10 where realized prices drift materially higher. Use a piecewise correction: modest adjustment for days 1–7, stronger cumulative uplift for days 8–30.",
    "Mean-reversion too strong: model reverts toward ~63–66 while realized series trends to ~68–70. Reduce mean-reversion strength when the 20–30d history shows a regime shift (higher highs/higher lows)."
  ]
}
